{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eo1BdwLuwEPDPOND4",
			"description": "Plasma Pistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Widely carried by Inquisitors, veteran officers and Astartes as a compact answer to armour a bolt pistol cannot beat; Black Library and Codex background repeatedly show plasma pistols overheating and injuring or killing careless users, a trait long associated with older, unstable patterns especially.\n\nDesign: Scaled down two dice from the plasma gun anchor (6dx4(3) burn ex) to 4dx4(3) burn ex for the standard, safe firing mode, keeping the same x4 standard / x5 supercharged multiplier pair used across every weapon in this file; the ×5 supercharged mode trades a Malf 14 risk for another 25% of damage, and the standard mode carries a lesser Malf 16 because this is an older, less stable pattern. Checked with the exact dice distribution: standard mode averages 56 damage and penetrates Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective DR 33) 95% of the time and a Terminator (DR 200, effective DR 66) 24% of the time; supercharged raises Terminator penetration to 56%. A pistol-class charge clears flak and carapace with no meaningful chance of failure either way. Handling: 6 lb loaded for the containment coil, capacitor and cooling fins a plasma weapon needs even at pistol scale - heavier than a bolt pistol's mechanically simpler cartridge action. Min ST 9† (√(10×6)≈7.7, bumped for the bulky coil housing and the two-handed brace most depictions show even for a \"pistol\") is below the plasma gun's ST 12, reflecting the smaller charge; the † still lets it be fired two-handed at the listed ST. RoF 1, not a pistol's usual 3: a plasma weapon must let its containment field cycle and vent excess heat between shots (framework.md's plasma-weapons rule), so even a pistol-format coil cannot be fired semi-automatically like a solid-slug or las sidearm. Shots 6(20): a small charge cell good for six shots before a slow 20-second swap, in line with the plasma gun's own scaled-down cell. Bulk -2 and Rcl 2 are ordinary pistol figures. Overheat: the malfunction is a fraction of the weapon's own charge, 2d×4(3) burn ex (avg 28): it kills an unarmoured user, badly hurts one in flak (97% penetrates), and mostly spares Astartes plate (28% penetrates) and Terminators (0%). Exact figures by dice distribution.",
