		{
			"id": "eS_GN5vZgY0W8ge2q",
			"description": "Plasma Gun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The plasma gun is the Guard's and the Astartes' standard answer to power armour and light vehicles alike; fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts to Space Marine Battles depicts it killing power-armoured targets outright while carrying a real chance of cooking its own wielder, especially on older, less stable patterns - the origin of the tabletop and RPG \"gets hot\"/ overheat mechanic this entry represents mechanically as Malf 16 (standard) and Malf 14 (supercharged).\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed plasma anchor: 6dx4(3) burn ex, treated as the weapon's standard mode, which the framework states kills Marines through power armour without needing to invoke overheating; it carries only a Malf 16 as an older, less stable pattern (the supercharged mode is Malf 14). Checked with the exact dice distribution, not just the average: Astartes power armour is torso DR 100; armour divisor (3) drops effective DR to 33, and 6dx4 averages 84, penetrating essentially every hit (99.9%), so it kills reliably as required. Against a Terminator's DR 200 (effective DR 66) it still penetrates 86% of hits, matching the framework's explicit statement that plasma \"penetrates Terminators more often than not.\" The supercharged mode (6dx5(3), Malf 14) bumps the multiplier one step further for harder targets (Mk X Gravis, multiple Terminators, light vehicles) at the cost of a real chance of the coil failing and burning the firer, matching the fiction's running theme of plasma weapons being feared by their own side almost as much as by the enemy. A malfunction does 3d×4(3) burn ex to the firer (avg 42): it kills an unarmoured or flak-armoured user outright, penetrates Astartes Mk VII 74% of the time (a wounded but living Marine, not a dead one), Gravis 50% and a Terminator 2%. The cannon and heavy incinerator (4d×4(3), avg 56) are worse: Terminator 24%. Shared pattern: Astartes carry this same weapon (Deathwatch shows the same guns), so it is one stat block, not a human/Astartes split. Handling: 14 lb loaded, per Only War/Rogue Trader's consistent depiction of a plasma gun as noticeably heavier than a lasgun for its coil, coolant jacket and capacitor bank. Min ST 12 (√(10×14)≈11.8, matching the framework's own worked figure for a weapon this weight almost exactly) needs both hands and real upper-body strength to control, well above a lasgun's ST 9 despite similar bulk, reflecting the reinforced housing a live plasma reaction demands. RoF 1 is the framework's explicit rule for plasma weapons - the coil has to recharge and vent heat between shots, so it cannot fire faster no matter how fast the trigger is pulled; a faster rate would ignore the weapon's actual mechanism. Shots 8(20): an 8-shot cell (Only War-style capacity) and a slow 20-second reload for a reservoir that has to be handled carefully. Bulk -4 and Rcl 2 (low, per framework.md's \"beams: 1\" figure nudged up slightly for the coil's own kick) are ordinary rifle-class figures.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
