		{
			"id": "eKHgSjbulJ6LgaJVK",
			"description": "Plasma Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A tripod- or vehicle-mounted heavy weapon fielded by Astra Militarum heavy weapon teams and Devastator squads, background consistently treats it as a slow-firing but devastating answer to Astartes-scale infantry and light vehicles at range, at the price of a low rate of fire while the reactor cycles.\n\nDesign: Two dice over the plasma gun anchor (8dx4(3) vs 6dx4(3), supercharged 8dx5(3)), matching the standard progression used for the bolt and melta families in this project. Checked against the vehicle table: standard mode averages 112 and, even against AV12 (effective DR 83), penetrates 94% of hits, comfortably beating the light and medium vehicles the fiction shows it killing. Handling: 45 lb loaded (excluding the 20 lb Heavy Weapon Tripod) puts it well beyond man-portable weight, and it is marked ST 13M (mounted): the tripod or pintle bears the bulk of that weight, so the ST figure covers recoil and aim rather than the raw √(10×45)≈21 a shoulder-fired weapon this heavy would need - the same weight as the Multi-laser (ST 9M) elsewhere in this project, pitched four points higher for the plasma reactor's own recoil kick, and a point under the 80 lb Lascannon's 14M because the Lascannon's barrel and power plant weigh far more. RoF 1 (unchanged from every other plasma weapon here - the reactor's cycle time, not the mount, is the limiting factor) and Malf 15 rather than the man-portable weapons' 14 reflect a crew-served weapon's better cooling and shielding, at correspondingly higher stakes for the crew when it does fail. Bulk -7 and Rcl 3 mark a genuine support weapon.",
