		{
			"id": "eL61SOulLgKLL-z1J",
			"description": "Plasma Incinerator, Primaris Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Standard-issue Primaris plasma weapon (Hellblaster squads and others), Codex background describes it as an improved, more reliable containment design over the legacy plasma gun rather than a fundamentally different weapon.\n\nDesign: One pip over the plasma gun anchor (6d+1x4(3) vs 6dx4(3), supercharged 6d+1x5(3); GCS reads the multiplier as applying to the whole roll, so (6d+1)x4) for the \"improved\" cartridge, on a lighter, easier-handling frame with better range (200/600) for the improved optics. Against a Terminator (DR 200, effective DR 66) the extra pip nudges standard-mode penetration from the plasma gun's 86% to 90%; the higher Malf 15 on its supercharged mode reflects the claimed better containment without pretending overheating risk is eliminated. Handling: 13 lb loaded, slightly under the legacy plasma gun's 14 lb for Codex's \"improved containment design\" claim; min ST 11 (√(10×13)≈11.4) follows accordingly - an easier-handling frame than the plasma gun's ST 12, matching an Astartes-issue weapon that a strong human could still shoulder at a penalty. RoF 1, same as every plasma weapon in this file (the containment coil still has to cycle and vent, improved design or not). Shots 10(20): a slightly bigger cell than the plasma gun's 8, per the \"improved\" reactor Codex text describes. Bulk -4 and Rcl 2 match the plasma gun's figures.",
