		{
			"id": "e_2yDeeS4KJbbR8dB",
			"description": "Heavy Plasma Incinerator, Primaris Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The two-handed, un-mounted heavy weapon carried by Primaris Hellblaster squads' heavy-weapon troopers, background treats it as a genuine step up in output over the standard plasma incinerator, manageable only because of a Primaris Marine's greater strength, not because the weapon itself is lighter.\n\nDesign: Matches the Plasma Cannon's damage (8dx4(3)/8dx5(3)) since both fire a cannon-class charge, but drops the tripod requirement entirely, reflecting that this is a man-portable weapon for a superhuman user rather than a crew-served support gun. Handling: 20 lb loaded - much lighter than the tripod-mounted Plasma Cannon's 45 lb, since this is a shoulder-fired weapon meant to be carried and fired by a single Astartes rather than braced on a mount. Min ST 14 (√(10×20)≈14.1) is set below the Plasma Cannon's mounted figure but well above the standard Plasma Incinerator's ST 11, reflecting real handling difficulty for anyone but an Astartes - a human could not reasonably shoulder it at all. RoF 1 (unchanged, per the family-wide plasma rule); the cell (8 shots) sits between the standard Incinerator's 10 and the Plasma Cannon's 5, and Malf 15 matches both, matching a weapon built as a scaled- down cannon rather than a scaled-up rifle. Bulk -5 and Rcl 2 reflect its real size without a mount to steady it.",
